+# TASK-260715-24icoz — tester verification results
+
+Date: 2026-08-19
+Role: tester
+Disposition: ready for review under the accepted acceptance-resume boundary
+
+## Outcome
+
+- Independently retrieved the retained archive and verified SHA-256 `daf0e1927999a369b49744f821414d8b56fd551fb0bf757925758fa83d358834`.
+- The archive contains exactly four regular executable members with unique canonical names and normalized root ownership metadata.
+- Re-ran the release inspector against the retained executable bytes using pinned Go 1.26.5. Format, machine architecture, CPU baseline, minimum runtime, linkage, executable mode, stripped/no-DWARF disposition, size, SHA-256, and report privacy all passed.
+- Rebuilt the four-target matrix from current `main` in an isolated clean-cache tester root and inspected it successfully. The current build also contained exactly four canonical executables and totaled 10,259,950 bytes. This compatibility build does not replace the retained accepted-commit assets.
+- Added two focused release-tool tests covering truncated/wrong-architecture binaries and the successful exact-budget/clean-checkout inspector branch. The release suite increased from 31 to 33 passing tests.
+
+## Retained bundle evidence
+
+Build identity: relay `0.1.0`, protocol v1, source commit `58676a23e2e0fb3fcc1b5005d59c6ed56d3c0096`, Go 1.26.5, release mode, `CGO_ENABLED=0`, internal linker, `-trimpath`, `-s -w`, no external debug companions.
+
+| Target | Format / machine | Bytes | SHA-256 | Runtime and linkage |
+| --- | --- | ---: | --- | --- |
+| `darwin/amd64` | Mach-O 64-bit / x86_64 | 2,623,664 | `783b94982e90f0ceed0af0fa11662d11a333e244b87256cbfa0f7d21695f3290` | macOS 12.0; libSystem and libresolv only |
+| `darwin/arm64` | Mach-O 64-bit / arm64 | 2,487,362 | `8ac45b257099c9d2079b0bd2cb9ae489acfb86e443ba7ca7e4b4b2a56380d64c` | macOS 12.0; libSystem and libresolv only |
+| `linux/amd64` | ELF64 little-endian / x86_64 | 2,592,894 | `ddcb22ed4d4a978992a04096abae8adc58d0b8bf3bcdc0c0a006775797e2941f` | Ubuntu 24.04 release fixture declaration; static, no `PT_INTERP`, `PT_DYNAMIC`, or libc |
+| `linux/arm64` | ELF64 little-endian / arm64 | 2,556,030 | `908b3d9ea3543b6144e2c99407c9aa02cc69e86c1cce80364d32dbdc3de8e0dc` | Ubuntu 24.04 arm64 release fixture declaration; static, no `PT_INTERP`, `PT_DYNAMIC`, or libc |
+
+Measured total: **10,259,950 bytes**. This measurement is handed to `TASK-260715-1tzaed`; using the measured total as an inspection equality ceiling is not shipping-budget ratification.
+
+## Rootless runtime evidence
+
+Both locally accepted baselines ran as unprivileged UID 502:
+
+| Target | Result |
+| --- | --- |
+| `darwin/arm64` native | Exit 0; canonical identity matched target, version, source commit, and exact self-SHA; protocol-v1 stdio emitted the exact 16-byte accepted server hello; stderr empty; clean EOF exit. |
+| `darwin/amd64` via approved Rosetta 2 | Exit 0; canonical identity matched target, version, source commit, and exact self-SHA; protocol-v1 stdio emitted the exact 16-byte accepted server hello; stderr empty; clean EOF exit. |
+| `linux/amd64` | Explicitly deferred to `TASK-260715-1c4l9v`; not recorded as pass. |
+| `linux/arm64` | Explicitly deferred to `TASK-260715-1c4l9v`; not recorded as pass. |
+| native Intel macOS | Explicitly deferred to `TASK-260715-1c4l9v`; Rosetta approval here does not claim native-Intel evidence. |
+
+## Validation commands and exit codes
+
+- Retained archive SHA/member inspection: exit 0.
+- Retained executable release inspection: exit 0.
+- Native arm64 identity and stdio smoke: exit 0.
+- Rosetta amd64 identity and stdio smoke: exit 0.
+- `make relay-toolchain-test`: exit 0, 33/33 tests passed.
+- `make relay-shell-test relay-shell-vet`: exit 0; all Go packages and vet passed using pinned Go 1.26.5.
+- Affected Python release-inspection coverage using the standard-library execution tracer: exit 0, 243/301 executable lines, **80.7%**.
+- Current-head `make -j4 relay-toolchain-build-all ...`: exit 0; exactly four target executables.
+- Current-head `inspect-assets`: exit 0; exact layout and binary policy passed.
+- Task-scoped Black check, Python compilation, ShellCheck, Actionlint, and `git diff --check`: exit 0.
+
+Unavailable or expected-negative attempts were not counted as passes:
+
+- `python3 -m coverage --version`: exit 1 because the optional module is unavailable; replaced by the standard-library trace measurement above.
+- `make relay-shell-coverage`: exit 2 because no such Make target exists; replaced by affected-code trace coverage.
+- `python3 -m black --check ...`: exit 1 because Black is installed as an executable, not a Python module. The installed `black` executable validated the two changed ranges with exit 0.
+- Running the retained inspector CLI from current `HEAD` with the retained source commit: exit 1 as designed (`source commit does not match checkout HEAD`). Direct retained-byte inspection then passed without falsifying checkout identity.
+- `task-board validate`: exit 1 due `EPIC-260715-2lz67t` remaining `to-dev` while its child aggregate is `development`. The attempted parent repair also exited 1 because that Epic is hard-blocked by unrelated `EPIC-260715-2mqgvm` (`reviewing`) and `EPIC-260715-3810we` (`backlog`). No unrelated dependency state was changed.
+
+## Tester conclusion
+
+The four retained bundle assets satisfy the task acceptance criteria under `TASK-260715-24icoz_acceptance-resume.md`: exact four-target layout, inspection and metadata evidence, rootless native-arm64 and approved-Rosetta runtime proof, honest deferred Linux/native-Intel rows, measured-size handoff, privacy-safe artifacts, passing tests, lint, and affected coverage above 80%. The board-wide parent aggregation anomaly is preserved for orchestration and does not invalidate relay evidence.
